--- Note: a genuine, PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED bug was hit and worked around here — see
    bug-vendor-csv-http-upload-broken.log. CSV uploads over real HTTP fail file-type detection
    (FastExcel casts the UploadedFile to string via SplFileInfo::__toString(), which returns the
    extension-less PHP tmp path, so `Str::endsWith($path,'csv')` is always false for a real upload
    and the CSV reader is never selected). XLSX uploads are unaffected (XLSX is the `reader()`
    method's default/else branch), so the live pass below uses XLSX fixtures generated via the
    same FastExcel package (import/export round-trip), which exercises the identical controller
    code path (collections -> the NEARS-1241 gate -> items/temp_products writes) end-to-end. ---

=== AC1 — live hijack attempt (vendor 2 attacking store 1's item id=1, alongside its own item id=2) ===
Pre-state:  items.id=1 "Sample Product"  price=10.00 store_id=1  (victim)
            items.id=2 "Red Apple"       price=3.50  store_id=2  (attacker's own)

POST /vendor-panel/item/bulk-import  button=update  products_file=hijack.xlsx
  rows: {Id:2, Name:"QA-1241-pwned-own", Price:99}, {Id:1, Name:"QA-1241-pwned-victim", Price:99}

Response: HTTP 302 -> /vendor-panel/item/bulk-import (back())
X-Request-Id: 5ee392f1-2c7e-4c53-884c-f7d9d5af9e74

Rendered toast (fetched the redirect target, grepped the Toastr script block):
  toastr.error('One or more items in this file do not belong to your store. No changes were made.','')
  <- exact match of messages.bulk_import_items_not_in_your_store, en. Generic: no ids/names leaked.

storage/logs/laravel.log (correlated by X-Request-Id -> correlation_id, confirms end-to-end join):
  [2026-09-07 22:46:38] production.WARNING: vendor item bulk update rejected: items outside the
  vendor store {"trace_id":"34108baca2a07f4a7c56c5a2607df5b3",
  "correlation_id":"5ee392f1-2c7e-4c53-884c-f7d9d5af9e74","item_ids":[1],"vendor_id":2}

Post-state (DB re-read past all scopes): items.id=1 UNCHANGED (name/price/store_id all identical
to pre-state); items.id=2 (attacker's own row) ALSO UNCHANGED — fails closed on the whole batch,
confirming AC1 live over the real HTTP/session/CSRF/file-upload stack, not just the phpunit harness.

=== AC2 — live happy path (vendor 2 updating only its own item id=2) ===
POST /vendor-panel/item/bulk-import  button=update  products_file=legit.xlsx
  rows: {Id:2, Name:"QA-1241-legit-own-update", Price:77}

Response: HTTP 302 -> /vendor-panel/item/bulk-import
Rendered toast: toastr.success('1 Products imported successfully','')
Post-state: items.id=2 -> name="QA-1241-legit-own-update" price=77.00 store_id=2 (unchanged store)
  -> ordinary in-store bulk update still works end-to-end; the gate does not over-block.

Fixture item 2 restored to its original name/price ("Red Apple", 3.50) immediately after this
check via a direct UPDATE on the ISOLATED per-worktree test DB (never the shared dev DB).

